          %title Gros toposes
          %h2#GrosToposes Gros toposes
          %p
            We have seen roughly two different kinds of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf+toposes"} sheaf toposes
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categories+of+sheaves+on+a+topological+space"} categories of sheaves on a given space
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                (Example
                = succeed ")," do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SheafOnATopologicalSpace"}
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localic+reflection"} localic reflection
                (Prop.
                = succeed ")," do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LocalicReflection"}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                in the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
                of
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/toposes"} toposes
              %p
                these are called
                = succeed ";" do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/petit+toposes"} petit toposes
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categories+of+sheaves"} categories of sheaves
                whose
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
                are
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+spaces"} generalized spaces
                (Example
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SmoothSetAnnounced"}
              %p
                these are called
                = succeed "." do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gros+toposes"} gros toposes
          #CohesiveGeneralizedSpacesAsFoundations.num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesion"} cohesive
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+spaces"} generalized spaces
                as
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/foundations"} foundations
                of
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometry"} geometry
            %p
              If we aim to lay
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/foundations"} foundations
              for
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometry"} geometry
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+spaces"} generalized spaces
              which have foundational
              %em a priori
              meaning, independent of an otherwise pre-configured notion of space. Hence we would like to first characterize suitable
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gros+toposes"} gros toposes
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/space"} space
              from these, and only then, possibly, consider the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localic+reflection"} petit topos-reflections
              of these (Prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LocalicReflection"}
              below).
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gros+toposes"} gros toposes
              of such foundational
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+spaces"} generalized spaces
              ought to have an
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+logic"} internal logic
              that knows about
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modalities"} modalities
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometry"} geometry
              such as
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+object"} discreteness
              or
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/concrete+object"} concreteness
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modalities"} modalities
              in Def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ModalOperator"}
              this leads to the definiton of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesive+toposes"} cohesive toposes
              (Def.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CohesiveTopos"}
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#PiecesHavePoints"}
              below, due to
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Some+Thoughts+on+the+Future+of+Category+Theory"} Lawvere 91
              = succeed ")." do
                %a{:href => "#cohesive+topos#LawvereAxiomatic"} Lawvere 07
