          .proof
            %h6#proof_3 Proof
            %p
              The comparison morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ptp
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ptp_{\mathbf{H}}
              is a special case of that discussed in Prop.
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ComparisonMorphismBetweenOppositeExtremes"}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ptp
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi H
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mtext is epi
                    %mphantom
                      %mi AAA
                    %mtext iff
                    %mphantom
                      %mi AAA
                    %msub
                      %mi ptp
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mtext is epi
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    ptp_{\mathbf{H}} \;\; \text{is epi}
                    \\phantom{AAA}
                    \\text{iff}
                    \\phantom{AAA}
                    ptp_{\mathbf{B}} \;\; \text{is epi}
                    \\,.
            %p
              In one direction, assume that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ptp
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ptp_{\mathbf{B}}
              is an epimorphism. By
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:PiecesToPointsFromBase"} (?)
              we have
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi ptp
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi H
                      %mo =
                      %mi Disc
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi ptp
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi B
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ptp_{\mathbf{H}} = Disc(ptp_{\mathbf{B}})
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Disc
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Disc
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
              and left adjoints preserve monomorphisms (Prop.
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LeftAdjointFunctorPreservesEpi"}
            %p
              In the other direction, assume that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ptp
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ptp_{\mathbf{H}}
              is an epimorphism. By
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:PointsToPiecesInTheBase"} (?)
              and
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:AdjunctOfptpH"} (?)
              we see that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ptp
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ptp_{\mathbf{B}}
              is re-obtained from this by applying
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Γ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma
              and then composition with isomorphisms. But
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Γ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma
              is again a left adjoint, and hence preserves epimorphism by Prop.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LeftAdjointFunctorPreservesEpi"}
            %p
              By applying
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:PointsToPiecesInTheBase"} (?)
              again, we find in particular that
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pieces+have+points"} pieces have points
              is also equivalent to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Π
                    %msubsup
                      %mi ϵ
                      %mrow
                        %mi Disc
                        %mi S
                      %mo ♭
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi \epsilon^\flat_{Disc S}
              being an epimorphism, for all
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                      %mo ∈
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \in \mathbf{B}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Hom
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Π
                    %msubsup
                      %mi ϵ
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi X
                      %mo ♭
                    %mo ,
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi Hom
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi H
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msubsup
                      %mi ϵ
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi X
                      %mo ♭
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Disc
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Hom_{\mathbf{B}}(\Pi \epsilon^\flat_{\mathbf{X}}, S)
                    \=
                    Hom_{\mathbf{\mathbf{H}}}(\epsilon^\flat_{\mathbf{X}}, Disc(S))
            %p
              being a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monomorphism"} monomorphism
              for all
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              (by adjunction isomorphism
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:HomIsomorphismForAdjointFunctors"} (?)
              and definition of
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/epimorphism"} epimorphism
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#Monomorphism"}
            %p
              Now by Lemma
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ReExpressingMiddleFunctorInAdjointTriple"}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Hom
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi H
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %msubsup
                      %mi η
                      %mrow
                        %mi Disc
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi S
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ♯
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Hom_{\mathbf{H}}( \mathbf{X}, \eta^\sharp_{Disc(S)} )
            %p
              being an injection for all
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{X}
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#Monomorphism"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi η
                      %mrow
                        %mi Disc
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi S
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ♯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta^\sharp_{Disc(S)}
              being a monomorphism, hence to
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+objects+are+concrete"} discrete objects are concrete
            %p This establishes the equivalence between the first two items.
          #CohesiveSiteSuchThatDiscreteObjectsAreConcrete.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_3 Proposition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesive+site"} cohesive site
                such that
                = succeed "/" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pieces+have+points"} pieces have points
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+objects+are+concrete"} discrete objects are concrete
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesive+site"} cohesive site
              (Def.
              = succeed ")," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#OneCohesiveSite"}
            %ul
              %li
                for every
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object"} object
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi 𝒞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in \mathcal{C}
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism"} morphism
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo *
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mo ∃
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \ast \overset{\exists}{\to} X
                from
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+the"} the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+object"} terminal object
                to
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom+set"} hom set
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Hom
                        %mi 𝒞
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo *
                      %mo ,
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Hom_{\mathcal{C}}(\ast, X)
                is
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inhabited+set"} non-empty
            %p
              Then the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesive+topos"} cohesive topos
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Sh
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh(\mathcal{C})
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CategoriesOfSheavesOnCohesiveSiteIsCohesive"}
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#PiecesHavePoints"}
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pieces+have+points"}> pieces have points
                  ,
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+objects+are+concrete"}> discrete objects are concrete
                  \.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_4 Proof
            %p
              By Prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#PiecesHavePoints"}
              it is sufficient to show the second condition, hence to check that for each
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi Set
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \in Set
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Disc
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi coDisc
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Disc(S) \longrightarrow coDisc(S)
            %p
              is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monomorphism"} monomorphism
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#RecognitionOfEpimorphisms"}
              this means equivalently that for each
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object"} object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in \mathcal{C}
              in the site, the component function
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Disc
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi coDisc
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Disc(S)(X) \longrightarrow coDisc(S)(X)
            %p
              is an
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/injective+function"} injective function
            %p
              Now, by the proof of Prop.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CategoriesOfSheavesOnCohesiveSiteIsCohesive"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagonal"} diagonal
              function
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi S
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi Hom
                              %mi Set
                            %mrow
                              %mo (
